<title>GERMANY: EAST GERMAN NOV ADJUSTED UNEMPLOYMENT RISES 17,000.</title>
<headline>EAST GERMAN NOV ADJUSTED UNEMPLOYMENT RISES 17,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour</p>
<p>Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Nov 96	 Oct 96	   Nov 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.117 mln    1.098 mln	1.043</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.176 mln    1.159 mln	1.095</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +17,000	+14,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		15.0 pct     14.7 pct	 14.0 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	44,489	 48,746	   60,187</p>
<p> Vacancies		   56,825	 58,551	   58,310</p>
<p> Change in number in work Sept 96	Aug 96</p>
<p>				 -3,000	 -4,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous</p>
<p>month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom, 49-228-609750</p>
</text>
